# Equipment macro id → static game stats.
#   slot, class    — slot is weapon/turret/shield/engine/thruster (what hardpoint
#                    it fits); class is the raw macro class (e.g. missileturret),
#                    kept alongside slot so the UI can tell those apart
#   name           — display name (identification ref, t-file resolved)
#   mk, size, race — mark, size class (s/m/l/xl), maker faction
#   price, price_min, price_max — average/min/max wares.xml buy price. The live
#                    in-game shop price can run above even price_max (reputation/
#                    station markup the static files don't capture) — treat as a
#                    range, not an exact figure
#   weapon/turret  — damage_hull, damage_shield, damage_hull_while_shielded (all
#                    per-shot, already scaled by barrels/pellets-per-shot),
#                    reload_rate (sustained shots/sec), range_m, projectile_speed_m_s,
#                    ammo_clip, ammo_clip_reload_s, rotation_speed, rotation_accel,
#                    hull_max (its own hitpoints), storage_capacity (missile bay,
#                    missileturret/missilelauncher only), damage_rate_burst,
#                    damage_rate_sustained, time_to_overheat, cooldown_duration
#                    (the last 4 are derived, matched against real tooltips —
#                    see gamefiles/generate_equipment.py's load_bullets/load_equipment).
#                    time_to_overheat is the UNMODIFIED weapon-only baseline (heat
#                    factor 1.0) — confirmed this session that it's also genuinely
#                    ship-dependent via SHIP_STATS' weapon_heat_factor, which the UI
#                    applies at display time once a hull is selected (see
#                    ui/js/sectors.js's weaponTipHtml). damage_rate_sustained and
#                    cooldown_duration are NOT affected by that factor.
#   shield         — capacity, recharge_rate, recharge_delay, disruption_stability
#                    (resistance to disruptor/ion shutdown — absent on "integrated"
#                    shields, which have no separate hull to disrupt), hull_max
#                    (the shield generator's own hit points — also absent when
#                    integrated)
#   engine         — thrust_forward, thrust_reverse, travel_thrust, boost_thrust
#   thruster       — strafe, pitch, yaw, roll
